{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550467-the-spirit-of-v20-and-opp-v5","id":1550467,"title":"The spirit of V20 and OPP V5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-28T17:08:22-07:00","id":1550467,"title":"The spirit of V20 and OPP V5","content":"This is going to be a post that mostly consists of gushing over OPP material. I think that every edition of VTM had its own &quot;flavor&quot; and themes that were very different from the ones that came before it and V20 was no different, especially when OPP got to releasing their own stuff. I also think it's why I liked their stuff for V5 and when they decided to go against the grain, I dropped off the edition.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, I think there's five things that OPP did that made it so successful.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Embracing the Silly but Smoothing it over</b>: OPP was never afraid to acknowledge even controversial bits of lore like the True Hand. Indeed, they made the True Hand WORK just by acknowledging they were just another Gehenna cult and full of assholes versus secret defenders of humanity.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Making a Wider World</b>: I don't think OPP was ever fond of things like the Kuei Jin anymore than modern WOD but it was certainly interested in a much more diverse broader WOD. The Drowned Legacies were an interesting possibility that could have applied to many other variations of Kindred across the globe. Maybe even move from the Caine myth to something more diverse like Requiem where vampires could have multiple origins.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Vampiric Arcanum and Mythology</b>: OPP really seemed a lot more interested in things like the Paths, vampiric secret history, Blood Cults (no kidding), and Spirituality than WW itself. Revised tried to dial back the Paths and Roads but V20 seemed to love them a lot more. They didn't automatically need to be pure evil but they were certainly DIFFERENT from mainstream Humanity.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Anarchs</b>: I don't think the Anarchs were ever something OPP was super into but they got a lot more respect in V20 than Third Edition. 5th Edition also took a lot of what made Anarchs unique and made them more like Diet Sabbat. I still think of Anarchs Unbound as one of the best. The Red Question was also one of the best ideas they ever came up with, IMHO<br /> <br /> 5. <b>They didn't try and tell you that your playstyle was wrong: </b>There was room in OPP's WOD to play as Elders, Neonates, Sabbat, Inconnu, True hand, or even Ahrimanes though I don't know why anyone would. They took the wheel and didn't try to invent it but offered all of the options up front in the main book. They didn't do indivdiual clanbooks but the much more economically friendly Lore of the Clans and Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> I have a bunch more praises I could sing but wanted to hear what you felt was the Spirit of WOD20?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T14:33:03-07:00","id":1550606,"title":"","content":"I liked that in later editions of how they explained how Kindred would gain influence on mortal society and how gentle they have to be and the reason for long term thinking of what people you should approach.<br /> <br /> For example Marcus Vitel wouldn't bother forming relationships with Presidents in 1600 Pennsylvania Ave as they will be gone by the 2nd term and would focus on people who would be still there despite administration changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T00:11:22-07:00","id":1550619,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I feel that much of the OPP material had the spirit of pastiche about it. The writers were attempting to continue the pre-existing game line, but heavily influenced by (in particular) the revised era, and not extending or challenging existing material, or even examining what the game line ought to be. To some degree, this was probably the result of the fact that they were producing licensed products, but the best one can say of many of the products is that they were workmanlike. I am primarily interested in the Dark Ages line, and the OPP products in this setting were an incredibly mixed bag; as appreciative as I am of new books, I can't say I was exactly excited by a new version of the Ahrimanes, or a playable Niktuku bloodline, or a badly-broken set of Roads and Paths, or all the Lasombra fan service.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T10:43:18-07:00","id":1550633,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that in the current setting is that the paths of enlightenment are not much of thing. I could never warm up to it all.<br /> <br /> Also I'm glad that in later editions that addressed on how to play a Malkavian better than what I heard in early versions when I learned the term FishMalk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-03-2025, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T14:52:58-07:00","id":1550640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550467-the-spirit-of-v20-and-opp-v5?p=1550633#post1550633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad that in the current setting is that the paths of enlightenment are not much of thing. I could never warm up to it all.<br /> <br /> Also I'm glad that in later editions that addressed on how to play a Malkavian better than what I heard in early versions when I learned the term FishMalk.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's always been a damned if you do, damned if you don't element.<br /> <br /> Treating the Malkavians as playful tricksters pisses off people who want mental illness treated seriously.<br /> <br /> However, a lot of writers then try to treat Malkavians as a bunch of psychotic killers and sociopaths, which is bigoted and vile against the mentally ill.<br /> <br /> And if you do neither...well, a lot of mental illness isn't very cinematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T15:10:20-07:00","id":1550642,"title":"","content":"I try to be mindful of mental illness as I have a couple of family members who battled with it. It's sad, tragic and scary, but it's not funny and I keep that in regards to my player character as his mental health issues is more subtle.<br /> <br /> Such as he really likes the color blue in his wardrobe and feels uneasy if he doesn't have that color on him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T06:13:46-07:00","id":1550657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550467-the-spirit-of-v20-and-opp-v5?p=1550640#post1550640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's always been a damned if you do, damned if you don't element.<br /> <br /> Treating the Malkavians as playful tricksters pisses off people who want mental illness treated seriously.<br /> <br /> However, a lot of writers then try to treat Malkavians as a bunch of psychotic killers and sociopaths, which is bigoted and vile against the mentally ill.<br /> <br /> And if you do neither...well, a lot of mental illness isn't very cinematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be cinematic. The point is, it doesn't have to define the character, either.<br /> <br /> The problem with both concepts in how they've been treated is that in both cases the character is reduced to their illness.<br /> <br /> A &quot;fishmalk&quot; isn't bad just because they're a trickster with mental a Derangement, but because the Derangement is the source of &quot;comedy&quot;. The same way, the problem with psychotic killers is that they're bad because their Derangement makes them bad.<br /> <br /> Good characters with mental illnesses are characters whose illness is just one aspect of them, even if this aspect sometimes plays a major role. The Voerman Systers in Bloodlines are a good example, they're complete characters with participation and stakes in the politics of the city, and they're neither Trickster or Psychotic Killer. And I dare you to say their Derangement isn't cinematic <b>when it mattered</b>, but most of the time it didn't need to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T06:30:15-07:00","id":1550658,"title":"","content":"Eh, I know I prefer playful trickster as a neuroatypical person with a family history that would give HP Lovecraft pause.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T14:27:47-07:00","id":1550670,"title":"","content":"I agree with liking that OPP tried to give players/Storytellers as many options as possible. Whether you like the Ahrimanes or not, it's a good thing that it's an option available to you.<br /> <br /> In that way, I appreciate OPP using their status as license-holders to act as good stewards of the World of Darkness. Regardless of what aspect of the setting it was, OPP generally tried to make it playable. As stated at the top of the thread, they brought back concepts like the True Black Hand, or Samual Haight. Two notorious aspects of early WoD that most old fans considered jokes or missteps. OPP made them <i>work</i>.<br /> <br /> You only see something being absent when there was just no good way to make it work, like the Kuei-Jin. And even then, they still danced around the existence of Kindred of the East, like with Beckett's Jyhad Diary and the sections devoted to the Ravnos. OPP didn't make rules for Kuei-Jin, but they kept the silhouette of vampires in Asia, for those who want to maintain the dynamic they have with other Vampire plotlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T09:14:43-07:00","id":1550691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550467-the-spirit-of-v20-and-opp-v5?p=1550640#post1550640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's always been a damned if you do, damned if you don't element.<br /> <br /> Treating the Malkavians as playful tricksters pisses off people who want mental illness treated seriously.<br /> <br /> However, a lot of writers then try to treat Malkavians as a bunch of psychotic killers and sociopaths, which is bigoted and vile against the mentally ill.<br /> <br /> And if you do neither...well, a lot of mental illness isn't very cinematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve always felt that the key to getting Malkavians right is to remember that they\u2019re not generic lunatics, they\u2019re MAD ORACLES - they\u2019ve been given uncommon insight into their world, but the fact that this is the World of Darkness means that this was a profoundly traumatic experience and leaves them struggling to find a new equilibrium between their insights and their trauma (With a variety of possible responses - some Malkavians are \u2018crazy sane\u2019 in that they cling to the prevailing models of normalcy until they become archaic to the point of eccentricity, others find them struggling with actual mental illness and yet others decide to set up shop in their Happy Place and never, ever leave it* whilst a few go DEEP in the quest for the transcendent).<br /> <br /> <br /> *Either embracing eccentricities and peculiarities that help them cope with their condition or just blatantly acting out (One suspect that \u2018Acting Out\u2019 explains quite a bit of \u2018Fish Malk\u2019 behaviour over the centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T09:21:14-07:00","id":1550692,"title":"","content":"Also, while I do like the notion of a more divergent vampiric population, some part of me has always felt that making the Curse of Caine just one possible explanation for vampirism amongst many other equally-valid possibilities would rob VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE of something integral to it\u2019s spirit.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, being able to say that \u201cVampires exist because God Does Not Like bloody murder\u201d is an excellent way to quietly suggest that cool vampire powers are all well and good, but the price is bloody murder (On a more punk note, I\u2019d bet money that at least a few fans of the setting were pulled in by the chance to whisper \u201cGod hates us so much he gave us Cool Vampire Powers - we can work with that\u201d).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T12:53:43-07:00","id":1550756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550467-the-spirit-of-v20-and-opp-v5?p=1550691#post1550691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve always felt that the key to getting Malkavians right is to remember that they\u2019re not generic lunatics, they\u2019re MAD ORACLES - they\u2019ve been given uncommon insight into their world, but the fact that this is the World of Darkness means that this was a profoundly traumatic experience and leaves them struggling to find a new equilibrium between their insights and their trauma (With a variety of possible responses - some Malkavians are \u2018crazy sane\u2019 in that they cling to the prevailing models of normalcy until they become archaic to the point of eccentricity, others find them struggling with actual mental illness and yet others decide to set up shop in their Happy Place and never, ever leave it* whilst a few go DEEP in the quest for the transcendent).<br /> <br /> <br /> *Either embracing eccentricities and peculiarities that help them cope with their condition or just blatantly acting out (One suspect that \u2018Acting Out\u2019 explains quite a bit of \u2018Fish Malk\u2019 behaviour over the centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also worth remembering that, in addition to the Actual Mental Illness, Clan Malkavian adds a completely separate layer of &quot;Performative Madness&quot;.<br /> <br /> They know well how lethal the Jyhad can be. As a bulwark against it, Malkavians will ACT more mentally ill than they really are. Layering on eccentricities - often inconsistently - to 1) make themselves seem like not a threat and 2) to hide their &quot;real&quot; mental illness they have a limited ability to suspend when the chips are down.<br /> <br /> Your enemies can't exploit your real, non-optional mental issue, if you clog their fact-finding ability with tons of affectations you can drop as convenient. Like a supervillain who pretends to have a weakness to lull their enemies into a false sense of security.<br /> <br /> Plus, Malkavians are immortal and bored. Maintaining an elaborate bit to fuck with people helps pass the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T14:38:04-07:00","id":1550763,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s definitely another way to add wrinkles to the Malkavian Clan Madness (Although I do wonder if a certain sort of Malkavian targets the mentally ill for an Embrace in the misguided belief that those already coping with a mental illness will have an easier time adjusting to a supernatural affliction - a somewhat dubious contention, to say the least).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T06:43:48-07:00","id":1550790,"title":"","content":"The Malkavians embrace for many reasons and certainly they do view the broken as having great potential for insight and opening up new vistas via the embrace for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T10:57:30-07:00","id":1550800,"title":"","content":"Of course whether the Malkavian in question is on the money or guilty of gross optimism must vary by the Embrace (If only because while \u2018Insight from Madness\u2019 is a pillar of Gothic and of Cosmic Horror, it\u2019s a somewhat dubious contention based on actual Real World scientific evidence, so it\u2019s<br /> important not to make it a dependable asset in the World of Darkness).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T11:22:05-07:00","id":1550804,"title":"","content":"They do shine like a beacon to the Malkavians, just as those with incredible insight about the world or having a certain degree of empathy might attract a sire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-08-2025, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T18:42:02-07:00","id":1550819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550467-the-spirit-of-v20-and-opp-v5?p=1550800#post1550800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course whether the Malkavian in question is on the money or guilty of gross optimism must vary by the Embrace (If only because while \u2018Insight from Madness\u2019 is a pillar of Gothic and of Cosmic Horror, it\u2019s a somewhat dubious contention based on actual Real World scientific evidence, so it\u2019s<br /> important not to make it a dependable asset in the World of Darkness).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's a dubious contention but so is vampires.<br /> <br /> The Malkavians madness comes with supernatural insight. Not regular people possessing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T19:18:27-07:00","id":1550821,"title":"","content":"I never played a Malkavian, but as a Storyteller I like the Seer and Trickster themes. I try to be careful about using them in too much of an exaggerated or stereotypical way, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T21:42:01-07:00","id":1550829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550467-the-spirit-of-v20-and-opp-v5?p=1550819#post1550819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it's a dubious contention but so is vampires.<br /> <br /> The Malkavians madness comes with supernatural insight. Not regular people possessing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Malkavians are and interesting and at times a challenging clan to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T12:22:39-07:00","id":1550848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550467-the-spirit-of-v20-and-opp-v5?p=1550819#post1550819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it's a dubious contention but so is vampires.<br /> <br /> The Malkavians madness comes with supernatural insight. Not regular people possessing it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Am I correct in understanding you to mean that (Even in the World of Darkness) madness only brings supernatural insights when it\u2019s the Clan Weakness of the Malkavians?<br /> <br /> If so then that tends to agree with my own ideas on the subject (Though given how very broken the World of Darkness can be, it\u2019s not hard to imagine those closest to the cracks in reality getting more of an eyeful than most).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T05:53:01-07:00","id":1550877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550467-the-spirit-of-v20-and-opp-v5?p=1550848#post1550848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I correct in understanding you to mean that (Even in the World of Darkness) madness only brings supernatural insights when it\u2019s the Clan Weakness of the Malkavians?<br /> <br /> If so then that tends to agree with my own ideas on the subject (Though given how very broken the World of Darkness can be, it\u2019s not hard to imagine those closest to the cracks in reality getting more of an eyeful than most).</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I look at it is actually that Malkav had insight first. Cain's curse coupled it with madness. Now the two are tied up <i>for Malkavians</i>, and yet not all Malkavians are significantly insightful, although they are all linked to the most insightful of them because of the Malkavian Madness Network. But it's not the madness that makes them insightful. It's the price they pay for it because Cain cursed them.<br /> <br /> Many other creatures, including vampires, have access to forms of insight in WoD, as you would expect since divination and premonition are already widespread phenomena in our world, let alone a world where the supernatural is presumed to be real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T13:15:28-07:00","id":1550890,"title":"","content":"Pretty much how I read it as that Malkav already was a seer before the embrace like Tziscme was. Caine cursed Malkav with madness for his role in the destruction of the 2nd generation or perhaps he learned things that he shouldn't about the Dark Father and this was his way of discrediting him before he could share it with his &quot;siblings&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T12:30:08-07:00","id":1550913,"title":"","content":"One thing that I like in later editions of the revised clan books is that had more nuanced characters and less annoying stereotypes such as the drug dealing Followers of Set clan member that came out of a bad exploitation film.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T15:22:26-07:00","id":1550918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550467-the-spirit-of-v20-and-opp-v5?p=1550913#post1550913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that I like in later editions of the revised clan books is that had more nuanced characters and less annoying stereotypes such as the drug dealing Followers of Set clan member that came out of a bad exploitation film.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my all time favorite Follower of Set was <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a>'s male model who was an abusive psychopath but in a very subtle charming way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T21:47:18-07:00","id":1550951,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a good concept CTPhipps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}